 "summary": "45 retro chip sound effects for RPG battle hits — 15 cues, up to 3 variants, loudness-matched OGG.",
 "description": "45 sound effects (15 cues, up to 3 variants each) in a consistent 8/16-bit console-style chip sounds: pulse and triangle waves, stepped volume, crushed noise. Silence-trimmed, loudness-matched per cue, peaks at -1 dBFS, OGG Vorbis 44.1 kHz.\nEvery sound is tagged with the engine cue it is made for (meta.oprnSound.slots), so the editor assistant can wire a whole set in one step.\n\nCues: battleStart, attack, attack-blunt, attack-pierce, attack-claw, damage, actorDamage, critical, miss, defend, faint, bossCollapse, escape, defeat, cast\n\nMade by code-based procedural synthesis — no samples, no recordings. OPRN procedural SFX.\n\nLicense summary: free to use, modify and ship in any game, commercial included; no resale or redistribution of the raw files as a sound library.",
